WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:02.065
- So yeah, my roommate just walked out

00:00:02.065 --> 00:00:03.214
and saw us playing Trump's board game,

00:00:03.214 --> 00:00:05.873
and I'm not sure that
I feel good about it.

00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:07.628
This is for a BuzzFeed video.

00:00:07.628 --> 00:00:10.378
- Nice. (laughs)

00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:15.357
- We're all coworkers at BuzzFeed.

00:00:15.357 --> 00:00:16.535
- We're friends.

00:00:16.535 --> 00:00:17.368
Sometimes...
- That's what it is.

00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:18.248
- That's what we are.

00:00:18.248 --> 00:00:20.630
The start of our friendship
was through games.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.654
Like, we had a board
game night after work.

00:00:22.654 --> 00:00:24.041
- Do we really want to broadcast that

00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:25.295
to the rest of the world?
- It's cute!

00:00:25.295 --> 00:00:26.543
Oh my god, we're such losers.

00:00:26.543 --> 00:00:27.376
(laughs)

00:00:27.376 --> 00:00:29.886
- I'd like to consider myself
a board game expert, yeah.

00:00:29.886 --> 00:00:31.126
(slowed down audio)

00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:33.316
If an expert means you win all the time,

00:00:33.316 --> 00:00:34.866
every board game you play, then yes,

00:00:34.866 --> 00:00:35.774
I'm a board game expert.

00:00:35.774 --> 00:00:37.317
- It helps when you
cheat all the time, too.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:39.234
- All right, calm down.

00:00:40.254 --> 00:00:42.826
- We are here to play
a mystery board game.

00:00:42.826 --> 00:00:43.984
- Oh, man.

00:00:43.984 --> 00:00:46.287
(tense music)

00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:47.120
- Oh (bleep).

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.413
- Oh, no.
- Oh.

00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:52.047
(triumphant music)

00:00:52.047 --> 00:00:52.880
- Yay.

00:00:54.113 --> 00:00:55.702
- I didn't even know he had a board game.

00:00:55.702 --> 00:00:56.535
- Mr. Trump, please.

00:00:56.535 --> 00:00:58.515
- My new game is Trump: The Game.

00:00:58.515 --> 00:01:01.182
(ambient music)

00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:09.400
- Is this just like Monopoly,
but everyone goes bankrupt?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.192
- [Scott] I'm back and you're fired.

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:12.372
- I don't know if you guys can see this.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.789
The age is adult.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.379
- It says, "It takes
brains to make millions.

00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:19.474
"It takes Trump to make billions."

00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:21.864
- [Scott] So does that mean
that Trump doesn't have brains?

00:01:21.864 --> 00:01:26.045
- It also has Trump's
face on all of the bills.

00:01:26.045 --> 00:01:28.314
- It's terrifying because
this is what money

00:01:28.314 --> 00:01:30.227
could look like in the future.

00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:31.227
- Oh my god.

00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:33.061
The pieces.

00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:34.538
- What are they?

00:01:34.538 --> 00:01:35.470
- Giant Ts.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.835
(laughing)

00:01:36.835 --> 00:01:38.926
The dice even have Ts on them.

00:01:38.926 --> 00:01:40.075
(laughing)

00:01:40.075 --> 00:01:42.918
(ambient music)

00:01:42.918 --> 00:01:43.790
- Ooh.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.623
- Wow, okay.

00:01:44.623 --> 00:01:46.272
- It's like a mini Monopoly board.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.298
- I mean, it's sorta pretty.

00:01:47.298 --> 00:01:48.131
- Wheel of Fortune.

00:01:48.131 --> 00:01:50.381
- It's not an ugly, well...

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.143
- The rule book.

00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:55.814
- Wow.

00:01:55.814 --> 00:01:57.464
- Ugh, that's so complicated.

00:01:57.464 --> 00:01:59.964
- Is this front and back, too?

00:02:01.304 --> 00:02:04.444
It starts with a contract
that Donald Trump signs

00:02:04.444 --> 00:02:06.982
just to say, "Now you're
about to play my game.

00:02:06.982 --> 00:02:09.482
"I invite you to the fantasy."

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.344
- It's even called a Trump card.

00:02:12.344 --> 00:02:13.844
Draw a Trump card.

00:02:15.519 --> 00:02:16.543
- Ah!

00:02:16.543 --> 00:02:18.023
I dropped one.

00:02:18.023 --> 00:02:20.665
- Half of my cards are about paying taxes.

00:02:20.665 --> 00:02:22.485
I guess you can play taxes
when you play his game,

00:02:22.485 --> 00:02:24.780
but not in real life.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.825
- It seems like you buy these properties

00:02:26.825 --> 00:02:28.511
and you invest money in them.

00:02:28.511 --> 00:02:31.217
It's just like a rip-off of
Monopoly in a lot of ways.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.496
- It's probably a shitty,
crappy, crappy game,

00:02:34.496 --> 00:02:35.747
but it might be fun.

00:02:35.747 --> 00:02:37.873
- No, I feel like it's very uninspired.

00:02:37.873 --> 00:02:40.493
- There's a lot of complicated
games we've tried to play

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:44.316
and they look absolutely
absurd, and yet they're okay.

00:02:44.316 --> 00:02:45.937
I still think we should give it a chance,

00:02:45.937 --> 00:02:47.125
I just don't think we've had enough time

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:49.315
to read the directions and
it's gonna take a long time

00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:50.563
to read the directions.

00:02:50.563 --> 00:02:52.221
- [Announcer] Trump: The
Game from Milton Bradley.

00:02:52.221 --> 00:02:53.386
- I think you'll like it.

00:02:53.386 --> 00:02:56.053
(comical music)

00:02:58.505 --> 00:03:00.653
- We covered it up just because
we were traveling with it.

00:03:00.653 --> 00:03:01.748
All right, I think we're here.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.533
We've got it properly set up this time

00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:05.033
and let's dive in.

00:03:11.445 --> 00:03:13.318
(blowing)

00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:14.605
(dice rolling)

00:03:14.605 --> 00:03:16.805
- [Stephen] Ooh, I got a
T, what does that mean?

00:03:16.805 --> 00:03:19.458
- Uh, the office building, up for auction.

00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:21.072
Stephen just bid way too much money.

00:03:21.072 --> 00:03:22.786
- He bid almost three times...
- What do you mean?

00:03:22.786 --> 00:03:25.872
- In 18 turns, you'll win your money back.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.337
- [Scott] You can come back from this.

00:03:27.337 --> 00:03:30.149
Guys, I got fired and I
wanna get back in this,

00:03:30.149 --> 00:03:34.736
but I can't, so I think Stephen
just won another building.

00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:38.334
- I do have to say, this is
actually not that bad of a game.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.899
It's actually kinda fun!

00:03:39.899 --> 00:03:42.982
- [Scott] Is this that bad of a game?

00:03:44.743 --> 00:03:45.701
- [Spencer] Is it one for me?

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:48.057
- I did not take his, I did
not take the Donald card!

00:03:48.057 --> 00:03:49.984
Do not let this lie come to.

00:03:49.984 --> 00:03:51.684
- Wait, I don't know if
he's lying, this is very...

00:03:51.684 --> 00:03:53.149
- I swear I don't have it!

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:54.303
- [Stephen] How long have we been playing?

00:03:54.303 --> 00:03:56.756
- We've been playing for almost two hours.

00:03:56.756 --> 00:03:58.359
- [Scott] This is gonna be it,
this is gonna end the game.

00:03:58.359 --> 00:04:01.456
- I'm counting our money
right now to see who won.

00:04:01.456 --> 00:04:03.284
- [Scott] Okay, Stephen,
how much money do you have?

00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:04.117
- Nine million.

00:04:04.117 --> 00:04:07.299
- Stephen has 900 million,
but what does Scott have?

00:04:07.299 --> 00:04:09.145
- [Stephen] If you won,
I'm gonna be so mad.

00:04:09.145 --> 00:04:12.018
- 880 million dollars.
- Oh my god!

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:13.573
- You almost beat Stephen then.

00:04:13.573 --> 00:04:14.846
- [Scott] I did almost beat Stephen.

00:04:14.846 --> 00:04:18.161
- I have one billion 340 million.

00:04:18.161 --> 00:04:19.359
- [Scott] What?

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.827
- [Stephen] Ah, you asshole!

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:23.789
- Yeah, I'm so excited.
- Oh my god.

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:25.778
- I never win games ever!

00:04:25.778 --> 00:04:28.089
- [Scott] And just look
at him there, fellas.

00:04:28.089 --> 00:04:30.823
Congratulations, you
are the next Apprentice.

00:04:30.823 --> 00:04:31.781
- No.

00:04:31.781 --> 00:04:34.448
(comical music)

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.423
- The game night went great because I won.

00:04:37.423 --> 00:04:39.492
- It was great 'cause Scott lost.

00:04:39.492 --> 00:04:41.050
- Yeah, and Scott lost, so it really

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.581
was a win-win situation for everyone.

00:04:43.581 --> 00:04:46.039
- No, maybe a win-win for you guys.

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:48.364
- It's not the best game,
it's not like the first ch-,

00:04:48.364 --> 00:04:49.197
I wouldn't be like, "Hey, guys,

00:04:49.197 --> 00:04:50.979
"let's play the Trump game, yeah."

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:52.117
I would give it probably like a,

00:04:52.117 --> 00:04:54.200
I don't know, a five, a six.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.033
Was that too high?

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:55.980
Do not judge me.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:56.891
- No, I was worried you were gonna say,

00:04:56.891 --> 00:04:57.724
like, eight or something.
- Yeah, I thought you were

00:04:57.724 --> 00:04:58.557
- gonna say an eight
- I would not

00:04:58.557 --> 00:04:59.390
- or a nine
- give it an eight.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:01.863
- Because I won, I'll give
it a three out of ten.

00:05:01.863 --> 00:05:04.258
- The Trump game shares a lot
of similarities with Monopoly,

00:05:04.258 --> 00:05:06.131
but it doesn't really deliver on them,

00:05:06.131 --> 00:05:08.685
and I think overall, it
would've been more successful

00:05:08.685 --> 00:05:10.931
to just have a Trump-themed Monopoly game.

00:05:10.931 --> 00:05:14.226
Like, I have Planet Earth
Monopoly and Nintendo Monopoly.

00:05:14.226 --> 00:05:16.928
That would just offer better
gameplay and an experience.

00:05:16.928 --> 00:05:19.431
I would probably do a
four or five out of ten.

00:05:19.431 --> 00:05:20.373
- That's pretty much where Trump's

00:05:20.373 --> 00:05:21.936
approval rating is at right now.

00:05:21.936 --> 00:05:23.980
(laughing)

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.028
- Sounds about accurate.

00:05:26.028 --> 00:05:28.695
(comical music)

